# The whole apparatus is hashed byte-for-byte into DIGEST, so Git must not rewrite any of it.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line normalization, so committed bytes survive checkout unchanged rather
# than being rewritten to the platform convention. Without this rule the recorded digest would not
# reproduce on a fresh clone, which would make the preregistered freeze unverifiable by anyone else --
# and two tasks additionally compare bytes exactly, so they would fail for reasons unrelated to the
# executor under test.
#
# fixture/.gitattributes repeats the rule so it still applies when the runner copies the fixture into
# a standalone repository for an attempt worktree.
* -text
